    "type": "WSI",
    "diagnosis": "Atypical apocrine adenosis. Fibrocystic changes",
    "title": "",
    "legend": "Atypical apocrine adenosis:\nVacuum assisted biopsy specimen shows several cores with an apocrine cell population superimposed on adenosis. Some of the apocrine cells show nuclear hyperchromasia and &gt;3 fold variation in nuclear size. Several ducts with apocrine change disclose a cribriform architecture, though luminal spaces are irregular and non-rigid. No comedonecrosis or obvious mitoses are found.",
    "source": "Tan Puay Hoon",
    "copyright": "",
